# versions.env — the pinned versions for the spark-rocky build.
# Bump here to stay current, then rebuild 01->04 and re-verify (see docs/build/build.md).

# Kernel SOURCE selector -- the which-kernel knob, so a build can A/B different kernels + configs.
#   kernelorg = stock kernel.org tarball (the v-major path 6.x / 7.x is derived from KVER).
#   clk       = CIQ Linux Kernel from GitHub (uses CLK tree's own aarch64 config; KVER derived from Makefile).
KERNEL_SOURCE=kernelorg
KCONFIG=config/rocky-6.18.34-gb10.config   # base .config (repo-relative); carries forward to KVER via olddefconfig. Point elsewhere to A/B another config.
# CLK commit to build from (only used when KERNEL_SOURCE=clk). The commit SHA is the content anchor —
# git object addressing; the tarball URL is commit-addressed — which is a WEAKER model than kernelorg's
# GPG-signed sha256sums: GitHub archive bytes are not guaranteed byte-stable, so no tarball hash can be
# pinned. KVER is derived from the fetched tree's Makefile (EXTRAVERSION empty on CLK stable branches).
# Branch: ciq-6.18.y-dgx-spark-config-tweaks
CLK_COMMIT=5a4e8f066adff7b394b39f717b1ff9e9eca354a2
KVER=6.18.38
DRIVER_VER=610.43.03
# SHA256 of NVIDIA-Linux-aarch64-$DRIVER_VER.run. NVIDIA publishes no signed checksums for the .run, so
# this pin is trust-on-first-download (TLS to us.download.nvidia.com + the .run's embedded `--check`
# self-test, both verified at bump time). What the pin buys: every rebuild consumes byte-identical driver
# input — a silent upstream re-roll or CDN tamper fails closed instead of silently changing the build.
# 02b verifies before extracting; 02c verifies before installing. Update when bumping DRIVER_VER.
DRIVER_SHA256=8d27655e8eb48a55cb2962af65f81b06756a558bb0eb38671ae883830c58cfde
ROCKY_RELEASEVER=10
# CUDA toolkit version for the IMAGE proof-of-life compiler (nvcc + cudart that validate.sh's vectorAdd uses).
# PINNED, not floating: held identical to the serving-container CUDA (13.0, #28) so the parity narrative in
# proof.md / software-stack.md stays true with zero edits, and a bump is a reviewable #26 diff -- never the
# silent package-name rot that 13-0 hardcoded in 02 used to be. This is NOT the parity CUDA; that lives in
# the digest-pinned serving containers and is out of scope for a live-USB release.
CUDA_VER=13-0
# Page size: an OPINIONATED, PINNED choice. 64k is our default for the GB10 concurrent AI-serving workload
# (measurable win on concurrent + deep-context cells; rationale + data in docs/build/platform-deltas.md).
# Build 4k by flipping this pin. The page size is a kernel CONFIG choice (CONFIG_ARM64_64K_PAGES), NOT a
# uname decoration: the kernel release stays plain $KVER (uname -r = 6.18.38) either way. 64k is proven by
# the config symbol + getconf PAGESIZE + the provenance stamp, and gated fail-closed in 05 -- not by a suffix.
PAGE_SIZE=64k
# SHA256 of linux-$KVER.tar.xz from kernel.org's signed sha256sums.asc (GPG-verified against the
# kernel.org autosigner key B886 8C80 BA62 A1FF FAF5 FDA9 632D 3A06 589D A6B1). 01-build-kernel.sh
# verifies the downloaded tarball against this before building (kernelorg only). Update when bumping KVER.
KERNEL_SHA256=ac26e508abd56e9f8b89872b6e10c49fc823bcc70d8068a5d8504c1a7c4ff045
